For substantive coding, proof, and writing tasks, read and use the installed
module-map-visuals SKILL.md as the default communication method, even when the
user has not explicitly requested a diagram. Use static ASCII/Unicode maps in
ordinary assistant messages: an initial map before substantial work, revisions
only for meaningful changes, and a final current-state map with scoped evidence.
Preserve the requested artifact and exact-output/accessibility exceptions.
Do not invoke viewers, animations, worker hooks, panes, or exports. This rule
controls communication only; it grants no new access or mutation permission.
